version: 2
title: How a version-2 playbook works
description: The playbook as one file — decisions and events, every document in it, and a walk that answers on screen and writes nothing.
events:
  - key: always
    label: Always
    trigger: imposed
    domain: Always
    detail: What holds at every moment — the shape of the file, how an answer picks a document, and where the engine lives.
    content:
      key: shape
      label: The shape of the file
      kind: brief
      doc:
        title: The shape of the file
        description: Two lists — decisions and events — and one document per event. The whole book is this one file.
        sections:
          - title: Top-level keys
            body: |
              `version: 2` on the first line, then, in the order a dump writes them:

              | key | what it is |
              |---|---|
              | `title` | the heading |
              | `description` | one line under the title |
              | `decisions` | the state space: questions, each with its answers |
              | `events` | what can happen, when it is on the table, what to do before its document shows, and the one document each shows when taken |

              Nothing else is read. What is always true is the content of an always-on event.
              The walk keeps its state in the host for the session and never writes it here.
          - title: Decisions
            body: |
              ```yaml
              decisions:
                - key: entity                  # identity — appears in every when and docs key
                  label: What are we?
                  values:
                    - key: none
                      label: Nothing yet
                    - key: company
                      label: A company
                      activates: [banking]     # an answer can bring a further question into being
                - key: banking
                  label: Where does the money sit?
                  values:
                    - key: personal
                      label: A personal account
                    - key: business
                      label: A business account
                      when: [entity=company]   # an answer offered only under another
              ```

              A state is an ASSIGNMENT — which answer is currently taken for each decision — and
              nothing in the file names one. Every decision opens unanswered. A decision with no
              `activates` pointing at it is always on the table; one that is activated exists only
              while an activating answer is taken.
          - title: Events
            body: |
              ```yaml
              events:
                - key: incorporate
                  label: We incorporate
                  trigger: chosen           # imposed (default) | chosen
                  arity: once               # once (default) | many
                  rate: 5/w                 # only meaningful with arity many
                  domain: Company           # a grouping heading in the rail, nothing more
                  detail: one italic line shown when the event is open
                  when: [entity=company]    # on the table only where this holds; absent = always
                  hint: markdown shown while an answer the document follows is open
                  content:                  # ONE entry — see below
                    kind: brief
                    doc: { title: The paperwork, sections: [...] }
              ```

              `trigger`: `imposed` arrives whether or not we are ready (a bolt); `chosen` fires
              when we say so (a hand). `arity: many` never leaves the table (a repeat icon, `rate`
              beside the label).
          - title: When and hint
            body: |
              Two optional fields on an event:

              - `when` — a condition over the assignment. The event is on the table only while
                every ref holds; absent, it is always there.
              - `hint` — markdown. While a `by` answer the document follows is unanswered, the
                pane shows it above "Answer … to see this": the ask. For an event with no
                content it is the response.

              The document shows once the answers it follows are taken; until then the hint
              does.
          - title: Content — one entry
            body: |
              An event's `content` is one mapping. `kind` names the engine that renders it, since
              there is no file extension to pick it from — `md`, `brief`, `guide`, `playbook`, any
              kind the Studio knows. Then either one document:

              ```yaml
              content:
                key: paperwork        # optional: what the walk collapses by
                label: The paperwork  # optional: the panel header; the key stands in
                kind: brief
                doc:                  # the document, exactly as a file of that kind would hold it
                  title: The paperwork
                  sections: [...]
              ```

              or a set that follows the answer:

              ```yaml
              content:
                key: paperwork
                kind: brief
                by: [entity]          # the decisions the set follows
                docs:                 # one document per answer combination, keyed
                  entity=none: {title: Nothing to file}                          #   decision=answer,…
                  entity=company: {title: As a company, sections: [...]}        #   in `by` order
              ```

              A document is that kind's YAML; for `md` it is a block string. A dump writes an
              entry as `key`, `label`, `kind`, `by`, `doc` or `docs`, each only when present. A `docs` set is
              CLOSED: every combination of the `by` answers is a member, written up front, and the
              checker lists the missing ones. With two decisions in `by` the key carries both
              segments in `by` order, `entity=company,banking=business`, and the set has one
              member per pair. Nothing is generated while walking — the answers only choose.
          - title: How an answer picks a document
            body: |
              For a `by` + `docs` entry, `variationOf(entry, locks)` takes the answer to each
              decision in `by`, in `by` order, into `segs`; the member shown is
              `docs[segs.join(",")]`. While any `by` decision is unanswered, `missing` names it and
              the pane shows the event's `hint` above "Answer … to see this." — an event
              whose document follows an answer carries the ask as its `hint`. A member is
              handed nothing: no answers, no context. A lone `doc` is itself whatever the
              answers.
          - title: What a document has not got
            body: |
              A path. Nothing is read from disk to show it, so it carries no annotations and is
              never pinned. What identifies it is its
              `key`, else its label, else where it sits (`event incorporate/0`).
          - title: One file
            body: |
              Everything the book shows is in the file: paste it, check it, render it with nothing
              else on disk. A document two books share is in each.
          - title: Refused
            body: |
              `doc` or `docs` without `kind` · `doc` and `docs` on one entry · `by` on a `doc` ·
              `docs` without `by` · a `docs` key that is not a combination of the `by` answers · a
              combination with no member · an `md` document that is not a string · a `content`
              list · a `file` on an entry.
          - title: Where the engine lives
            body: |
              `packages/filekinds/src/lib/playbookDoc.ts` — `parsePlaybook`, `dumpPlaybook`,
              `versionProblems`, `inlineProblems`, `variationOf`, `variationKeys`, `writtenDoc`,
              `contentKey`, `contentPath`, `contentText`, and the derivation: `meets`,
              `activeDecisions`, `impliedLocks`, `pruneLocks`, `take`, `rulesOf`
              (at version 2, each event as its own rule — its `when` and `hint`),
              `ruleFor`, `canArise`, `eventsAt`. Its header comment is what
              `studio-check --spec playbook` prints.
              `docVersion.ts` beside it reads the version line. The walk is
              `components/playbook/PlaybookWalk.tsx`, the session state is `PlaybookPreview.tsx`,
              the checker is `python/studio_kinds/kinds/playbook.py`. The engine is mirrored to the public
              `studio-kinds` repository by `pnpm kinds:sync`.
  - key: opened
    label: The file is opened
    trigger: imposed
    domain: Opening
    detail: parsePlaybook reads the YAML once; the walk is drawn with every decision unanswered.
    content:
      key: parse
      label: What the parser keeps
      kind: md
      doc: |
        `readDocVersion` reads `version:` off the root, then `parsePlaybook` reads `title`,
        `description`, `decisions` and `events`. On each event, `when` and `hint` are kept
        when present. For each event's `content`:

        - `key`, `label` — kept when present.
        - `kind` — lower-cased, a leading dot dropped (`.brief` and `brief` are the same).
        - `by` — kept when present.
        - `doc` / `docs` — kept as parsed YAML, whatever shape; the kind's own engine judges it.

        Dropped, and named by `versionProblems`: an entry that names a `file`, an entry with
        neither `doc` nor `docs`. A `content` list is read as its first entry so the walk still
        shows something, and the list is named.

        Parsing never throws: an unreadable file opens as an empty playbook, an unknown key is
        ignored, `trigger` defaults to `imposed`, a missing `key` is slugged from the label. The
        walk opens with nothing answered: the rail shows every decision with no `activates`
        pointing at it, and the events that can arise under an empty assignment, grouped by
        `domain` in the order the domains first appear.
  - key: answered
    label: An answer is taken
    trigger: chosen
    arity: many
    domain: Walking
    detail: The host keeps the assignment for the session; the file is untouched.
    content:
      key: session
      label: Session-only
      kind: md
      doc: |
        A pill click replaces any other answer to the same decision, then `pruneLocks` drops
        answers to questions no longer on the table, to a fixed point. `impliedLocks` takes any
        decision down to one available answer without showing it. The rail and the events on
        the table recompute from the new assignment — `eventsAt` keeps the events whose `when`
        holds (`canArise`), a `by` entry picks its member.

        `PlaybookPreview` holds the assignment and the folded panels in its own state
        and never calls the host's `onChange`. The YAML does not change; reload the file and every
        decision is unanswered again. Two consequences: a hand edit and a click can never fight
        over the file, and a standing answer cannot be stored in the book — what the book holds is
        the questions and what to do under each answer; the answer itself is given elsewhere, each
        time.
  - key: event-clicked
    label: An event is clicked
    trigger: chosen
    arity: many
    domain: Walking
    detail: The event-detail table picks the body; the document renders by its kind.
    content:
      key: detail
      label: What the pane shows
      kind: brief
      doc:
        title: What the pane shows
        description: One body per event, decided by the event-detail table, then rendered without a read.
        sections:
          - title: Which body
            body: |
              A click SELECTS the event; its content shows in the pane, never inline in the rail,
              so there is nothing to collapse; a second click only brings the pane back into view
              on a narrow screen. The event is its own rule (`rulesOf`): its `hint`
              applies whenever it is on the table. The pane stacks the `detail` line, then
              ONE body from the `event-detail` table (`eventDetailRules.ts`):

              | content | body |
              |---|---|
              | an entry with all its `by` answers taken | that document, bare — no card, no header, filling the pane |
              | an entry with a `by` answer open | the event's `hint`, then "Answer … to see this." |
              | none, and the event has `hint` | the hint prose, rendered as markdown |
              | none, and no hint | "No response recorded — this is a hole, not a nothing." |

              An event has one entry, so there is never a list of cards.
          - title: From `doc` to a renderer
            body: |
              `contentPath(entry)` is `inline.<kind>` — a synthetic name the file-kind registry
              picks a renderer from exactly as it would for a real `x.<kind>` file. `contentText`
              is the chosen document dumped back to YAML (`js-yaml`), or the string itself for
              `md`. The panel (`ContentPanel` in `PlaybookWalk.tsx`) takes that text beside the
              path and performs no read, so the book renders in a host that has no directory.
              Folding a panel is remembered in the session under the entry's `key`; a set's panel
              is keyed by the entry plus its segments, so it remounts when the answers pick
              another member.
  - key: checked
    label: studio-check runs on it
    trigger: imposed
    domain: Writing
    detail: One file in, one verdict out — and a verdict per document in it.
    content:
      key: checker
      label: What the checker does
      kind: brief
      doc:
        title: What the checker does
        description: The order it runs in, the summary line, and what it leaves alone.
        sections:
          - title: In order
            body: |
              1. Parse — a YAML error is the only problem reported.
              2. `versionProblems` — the version line, then a `content` list, a `file` on an
                 entry.
              3. `legacyProblems` — keys the format no longer has: `library`, `compare`, topic
                 `variants`, `materials`, `scales`, `view.against`, `view.tab`, `view.thresholds`.
              4. `variationProblems` — every decision in every `by` is a decision of this book.
              5. `inlineProblems` — `doc`/`docs` without `kind`; both on one entry; `by` on a
                 `doc`; `docs` without `by`; a `docs` set that is not exactly the closed set of
                 its `by` answers; an `md` document that is not a string.
              6. Each document through its own kind's check, named
                 `event <key>: <label> (<kind>)` and, for a set member, `[<segments>]`.
          - title: The summary line
            body: |
              `v2 · N decisions, N events, N documents` — the last count is the events with
              content; a set counts once.
          - title: Not checked
            body: |
              That the prose is true. That refs in an event's `when` name real
              decisions and answers — a stale `when` never holds, quietly, and the event never
              appears.
  - key: authored
    label: A book is written
    trigger: chosen
    domain: Writing
    content:
      key: write
      label: Writing one
      kind: guide
      doc:
        title: Write a playbook
        description: From the template to a file the checker passes — one file, start to finish.
        steps:
          - key: template
            label: Start from the template
            detail: |
              `studio-check --template playbook > new.playbook`. The first line is `version: 2`;
              leave it.
          - key: decisions
            label: Write the decisions
            after: [template]
            detail: |
              One per question whose answer changes what is on the table. Keys are identity: they
              appear in every `when` and `docs` key. A question that exists only under an
              answer goes in that answer's `activates`; an answer offered only under another gets
              its own `when`. No answer is written anywhere — the book opens unanswered every time.
          - key: events
            label: Write the events
            after: [template]
            detail: |
              `trigger: chosen` when we decide it happens, `imposed` when the world does; `domain`
              groups them in the rail; `arity: many` for something that recurs and never finishes.
              Then, on the event, only what applies: `when` where it is on the table only under
              an answer; `hint` — the ask — where
              its document follows an answer, or the response where it shows nothing.
          - key: content
            label: Write each document in
            after: [events]
            detail: |
              `content:` as a mapping — `kind: <kind>`, then `doc:` holding the document exactly
              as a file of that kind would: `title` and `sections` for a brief, `steps` for a
              guide, a block string for `md`. Indentation is the only
              thing to get right.
          - key: members
            label: Write a set where the document follows an answer
            after: [content]
            detail: |
              `by: [decision]` and `docs:` with one member per answer, keyed `decision=answer`
              (two decisions in `by`: one member per pair, `a=x,b=y`, in `by` order). Write every
              member; the checker lists the ones missing.
          - key: check
            label: Check it
            after: [decisions, members]
            detail: |
              `studio-check new.playbook`. Exit 1 names what is refused and what each
              document's own engine found. The file needs nothing beside it.
